  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Creation of Sustainable Agriculture Models for the Purpose of Enhancing Food Security, Biodiversity and Forest Cover in North-West, Haiti (Phase 2)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OPA will train members of approximately 10 farmer associations in the first and third communal sections of Port-de-Paix in northwest Haiti in agroforestry systems and improved agricultural production. It will establish approximately 10 seed banks and strengthen the organizations&apos; management. Farmers will run two tree nurseries and maintain about 40 demonstration plots. Approximately 220 farmers will benefit directly and another 2,200 farmers and their families will benefit indirectly.</narrative>
  </description>
